// Title: Arbitrary File Download Via GfxDownloadWrapper.EXE
// Sigma ID: eee00933-a761-4cd0-be70-c42fe91731e7
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Victor Sergeev, oscd.community
// Date: 2020-10-09 | Modified: 2023-10-18
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1105
// Description: Detects execution of GfxDownloadWrapper.exe with a URL as an argument to download file.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/HonorableMentions/GfxDownloadWrapper/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_gfxdownloadwrapper_arbitrary_file_download.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\GfxDownloadWrapper.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "http://" or ProcessCommandLine contains "https://")) and (not(ProcessCommandLine contains "https://gameplayapi.intel.com/"))
